delta-change "language-bootstrap"
message "install LanguageBootstrap TemplateGrammar and DeltaLanguageBootstrap product layer over frozen F11"
author "trellis-product"
doc "guide" """
  |# LanguageBootstrap / TemplateGrammar / ΔLanguageBootstrap
  |
  |This is the first product layer above the frozen F0–F11 bootstrap constitution. It is not F12.
  |
  |`LanguageBootstrap.delta` depends on the frozen F11 change and derives a product graph without modifying `Bootstrap.graph` or any foundation identity.
  |
  |## What is graph data
  |
  |The product graph defines:
  |
  |- `language-bootstrap.schema` — vocabulary for object-language definitions;
  |- `template-grammar.schema` — vocabulary for interpreted bidirectional prefix grammars;
  |- `delta-language-bootstrap.schema` — the free change schema associated with LanguageBootstrap artifacts;
  |- the concrete `Bool0` language, its `Expr` sort and four constructors;
  |- the concrete `Bool0Grammar` with four production templates;
  |- `DeltaBool0`, a free specialization of constitutional `DeltaTrellis`;
  |- graph-defined change operators including `replace-preserving-edges`.
  |
  |The example grammar is intentionally tiny:
  |
  |```text
  |Expr := true
  |      | false
  |      | not Expr
  |      | and Expr Expr
  |```
  |
  |The graph stores these as production templates:
  |
  |```text
  |lit:true
  |lit:false
  |lit:not;ref:value:Expr
  |lit:and;ref:left:Expr;ref:right:Expr
  |```
  |
  |## What remains host machinery
  |
  |`Language.scala` supplies a small generic interpreter. It discovers the language, grammar, constructors, productions, and associated change language through typed graph edges. It knows how to interpret the TemplateGrammar template vocabulary, but contains no `Bool0` parser cases.
  |
  |Parsing and printing use the same production set, giving the initial laws:
  |
  |```text
  |parse(print(ast)) = ast
  |print(parse(text)) = normalizeWhitespace(text)
  |```
  |
  |for unambiguous TemplateGrammar inputs.
  |
  |## Free changes
  |
  |Every object language must have exactly one associated `language.change-language`. `DeltaBool0` declares `basis = DeltaTrellis` and exposes the underlying free generators used for semantic edits.
  |
  |`replace-preserving-edges` is derived tooling: it disconnects incident semantic edges, replaces an entity, and reconnects equivalent ports to the replacement content. Admission is fail-closed and revalidates both the constitutional graph laws and LanguageBootstrap laws.
  |
  |A test changes the `true` production to `yes` entirely through graph data. The generic parser then accepts `yes` and rejects `true` without parser code changes.
  |
  |## Frozen constitution boundary
  |
  |The product layer is deliberately separate:
  |
  |```text
  |F0 ... F11             frozen constitution
  |       |
  |       + LanguageBootstrap.delta
  |              |
  |              v
  |   LanguageBootstrap product graph
  |```
  |
  |`Bootstrap.graph` remains exactly the frozen F11 graph.
  |

  """
test "canonical delta contract"
  assert "canonical"
  assert "valid"
  assert "source-roundtrip"
  assert "dependency" "@6aa7aabb086c5b6c02574b05495a2dcc67d6fb32cbaf5048ca728926a85e78c5"
  assert "introduces" "language-bootstrap.schema" "language.schema"
depends "@6aa7aabb086c5b6c02574b05495a2dcc67d6fb32cbaf5048ca728926a85e78c5"
  replace "language-bootstrap.schema" "language.schema"
    port "self" "out" "3:cap4:meta12:unrestricted14:4:atom6:Schema6:4:none"
    attr "description" "graph-resident schema for defining object languages"
    attr "name" "LanguageBootstrap"
    attr "slice" "LanguageBootstrap"
  replace "template-grammar.schema" "grammar.schema"
